- Install engine after the first VM test: a mount namespace and a
  session keyring of its own (cr_root is not kept busy, sdbootutil finds
  its keys under sudo), wipefs before systemd-repart (installing over an
  earlier install), keyring entries dropped whatever happens, no
  systemd-growfs on the read-only snapshot. TPM2 is sealed on the first
  boot of the new system (sdbootutil-enroll.service): the live boot's
  measurements cannot predict it. Require the TSS libraries systemd loads.
- sdbootutil with --disable-predictions for TPM2 (the first boot
  predicts), the GPT "grow file system" attribute cleared with sfdisk,
  no control characters in the error shown at step 13.

